Much love, I'll see you soon.

00:14:09.218 --> 00:14:10.979
- When you think about
that person in your life

00:14:10.979 --> 00:14:12.863
and usually people have
someone they're like, oh

00:14:12.863 --> 00:14:14.125
I know the difficult person.

00:14:14.125 --> 00:14:14.958
- Right.

00:14:14.958 --> 00:14:16.873
- The first step is to identify which type

00:14:16.873 --> 00:14:17.765
do they fall into.

00:14:17.765 --> 00:14:19.677
There's four main types
of difficult people.

00:14:19.677 --> 00:14:21.435
And by the way, on our worst day,

00:14:21.435 --> 00:14:23.614
we all fall into one of these types.

00:14:23.614 --> 00:14:24.637
- Oh that's right.
- Okay.

00:14:24.637 --> 00:14:26.731
So one might sound familiar.

00:14:26.731 --> 00:14:28.766
So the first one is downers,

00:14:28.766 --> 00:14:31.916
so negative Nancies, Debbie downers.

00:14:31.916 --> 00:14:34.278
They complain, they come
in the room and it's like

00:14:34.278 --> 00:14:35.970
the energy just drops out of there.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.221
- Absolutely.
- They complain a lot

00:14:37.221 --> 00:14:39.145
that kind of bucket.
- Right.

00:14:39.145 --> 00:14:41.629
- The second bucket is better thans.

00:14:41.629 --> 00:14:43.557
So these are show-offs,

00:14:43.557 --> 00:14:45.499
people who name-drop.

00:14:45.499 --> 00:14:47.159
I always hit a one-up.

00:14:47.159 --> 00:14:48.045
So.
- Oh yeah.

00:14:48.045 --> 00:14:49.296
- You know like.

00:14:49.296 --> 00:14:51.020
- You have a story you went
to Italy and blah-de-blah.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.020
And then someone said, oh yeah.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:53.972
- I went to Italy longer.

00:14:53.972 --> 00:14:55.246
- Right.
- It was even better.

00:14:55.246 --> 00:14:56.157
- Right.
- So they always like

00:14:56.157 --> 00:14:57.306
if you have something good
they have something better.

00:14:57.306 --> 00:14:58.437
If you have something big,
they have something bigger.

00:14:58.437 --> 00:14:59.558
- Right.
- One up.

00:14:59.558 --> 00:15:00.856
- Got it.
- And they name drop

00:15:00.856 --> 00:15:04.576
things, they just they, when
people feel low confidence

00:15:04.576 --> 00:15:07.037
this is what they do to
make themselves feel better

00:15:07.037 --> 00:15:08.574
They feel like they
have to be better than.

00:15:08.574 --> 00:15:09.805
- Right.
- Okay so the third type

00:15:09.805 --> 00:15:10.859
are passes.

00:15:10.859 --> 00:15:13.445
So this happens typically when
people are so low confident

00:15:13.445 --> 00:15:15.369
that they don't have a voice.

00:15:15.369 --> 00:15:17.272
So they don't make decisions.

00:15:17.272 --> 00:15:18.596
Right, you ask them, "So
what do you want to do?"

00:15:18.596 --> 00:15:20.053
"Whatever you want."
- Right.

00:15:20.053 --> 00:15:21.990
- They can be a little
difficult a little difficult

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:22.983
in conversation.

00:15:22.983 --> 00:15:24.504
You ask them a question
they have a one-word answer.

00:15:24.504 --> 00:15:25.337
- Right.

00:15:25.337 --> 00:15:26.274
- They don't ask you anything back.

00:15:26.274 --> 00:15:27.745
They're very passive.

00:15:27.745 --> 00:15:29.276
And it's usually because they're afraid,

00:15:29.276 --> 00:15:30.163
they don't think they're worth it.

00:15:30.163 --> 00:15:32.033
- Right.
- The fourth

00:15:32.033 --> 00:15:34.283
difficult type of person is

00:15:35.126 --> 00:15:37.836
downers, passives, uppers

00:15:37.836 --> 00:15:39.436
oh and tanks.

00:15:39.436 --> 00:15:40.269
Yeah.

00:15:40.269 --> 00:15:42.542
So tanks are the ones where they can get

00:15:42.542 --> 00:15:45.105
really angry, kind of explosive.

00:15:45.105 --> 00:15:46.855
They can be called bossy, which I think

00:15:46.855 --> 00:15:48.234
is a banned word these days.

00:15:48.234 --> 00:15:49.067
- Right.

00:15:49.067 --> 00:15:50.204
- We're not supposed to use bossy,

00:15:50.204 --> 00:15:51.055
we're not supposed to use bossy.

00:15:51.055 --> 00:15:52.358
So they kind of come
in and they want to be

00:15:52.358 --> 00:15:53.191
a control freak.

00:15:53.191 --> 00:15:54.505
They're like I want to take
control of the situation.

00:15:54.505 --> 00:15:55.468
- Yeah.
- So they can

00:15:55.468 --> 00:15:56.748
be very emotional.

00:15:56.748 --> 00:15:58.962
That's the cue you want to watch out for.

00:15:58.962 --> 00:16:00.947
So once you identify the type of person

00:16:00.947 --> 00:16:03.186
that you're dealing with the second step

00:16:03.186 --> 00:16:04.669
and this is the biggest mistake,

00:16:04.669 --> 00:16:06.369
is, you can't try to fix them.

00:16:06.369 --> 00:16:07.442
- Right.
- Right.

00:16:07.442 --> 00:16:09.090
- You have to adjust to them, don't you?

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:10.034
- Right, you adjust to them.

00:16:10.034 --> 00:16:13.237
The problem is is if you try
to tell a tank to calm down

00:16:13.237 --> 00:16:14.806
they usually freak out even more.

00:16:14.806 --> 00:16:15.639
- Right.

00:16:15.639 --> 00:16:17.029
- If you tell a passive to speak up

00:16:17.029 --> 00:16:17.978
that makes them even more shy.

00:16:17.978 --> 00:16:18.811
- Right.

00:16:18.811 --> 00:16:19.702
- So if you try to fix them

00:16:19.702 --> 00:16:21.846
that usually makes them
even more uncomfortable.

00:16:21.846 --> 00:16:22.679
- Sure.

00:16:22.679 --> 00:16:23.968
- So the better thing to do is step three

00:16:23.968 --> 00:16:26.380
and that's to try to understand them.

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:28.692
So if you can shift the mindset from,

00:16:28.692 --> 00:16:29.914
I don't want to fix them or change them,

00:16:29.914 --> 00:16:31.604
I want to understand
where they're coming from,

00:16:31.604 --> 00:16:34.382
I call this finding their value language.

00:16:34.382 --> 00:16:37.174
So everyone has a value language.

00:16:37.174 --> 00:16:40.740
This is something that they
in it drives their actions.

00:16:40.740 --> 00:16:42.152
It's what they hold most dear.

00:16:42.152 --> 00:16:44.110
So it could be knowledge,

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.443
they want to know everything.

00:16:45.443 --> 00:16:48.306
Or it could be money that they want

00:16:48.306 --> 00:16:49.983
huge amounts of financial success.

00:16:49.983 --> 00:16:52.495
- Do they all have the
same kind of language?

00:16:52.495 --> 00:16:53.807
I mean does the tank always

00:16:53.807 --> 00:16:55.261
have the same kind of language?

00:16:55.261 --> 00:16:57.342
- So typically like better
thans are know-it-alls.

00:16:57.342 --> 00:16:58.175
- Okay.

00:16:58.175 --> 00:16:59.608
- Typically that goes
long, but not always.

00:16:59.608 --> 00:17:02.150
Typically passives usually they want

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:04.377
to be in control of their relationships.

00:17:04.377 --> 00:17:05.210
- Okay.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:07.092
- So like to know the people in the room.

00:17:07.092 --> 00:17:08.938
So figure out, and you can do this by

00:17:08.938 --> 00:17:10.705
asking really open-ended questions,

00:17:10.705 --> 00:17:12.765
to figure out what is driving them.

00:17:12.765 --> 00:17:15.238
That will usually calm them down.

00:17:15.238 --> 00:17:16.498
- Well give me an example of a question

00:17:16.498 --> 00:17:17.686
I would ask a tank, say.

00:17:17.686 --> 00:17:18.967
- Sure, so let's say that you have a tank

00:17:18.967 --> 00:17:20.864
and you can see that they're
kind of in control mode

00:17:20.864 --> 00:17:21.697
when they're walking around,

00:17:21.697 --> 00:17:22.530
they're trying to control everything.

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:24.221
You can say, "So tell me

00:17:24.221 --> 00:17:25.563
"what's been going on for you?"

00:17:25.563 --> 00:17:27.347
Or instead of asking like,
"How are you doing?",

00:17:27.347 --> 00:17:28.911
or, "How's work?", you can say,

00:17:28.911 --> 00:17:30.654
"So are there any issues
that are bothering you?",

00:17:30.654 --> 00:17:32.997
or, "What personal passion
projects are you working on?"

00:17:32.997 --> 00:17:34.316
- Okay.
- Those kind of deeper

00:17:34.316 --> 00:17:36.138
questions can usually get them out of

00:17:36.138 --> 00:17:38.190
that overbearing mode

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:39.778
and into discussion with you.

00:17:39.778 --> 00:17:42.098
And that leads you
perfectly into the fourth.

00:17:42.098 --> 00:17:44.684
So you've identified the type.

00:17:44.684 --> 00:17:47.007
You've said you're not going to fix them.

00:17:47.007 --> 00:17:48.409
You are trying to understand them,

00:17:48.409 --> 00:17:50.858
the last one is to make sure
they're not toxic to you.

00:17:50.858 --> 00:17:51.691
- Oh good point.

00:17:51.691 --> 00:17:53.736
- Right so this is all about you now.

00:17:53.736 --> 00:17:57.219
So making sure you have
boundaries set on time sets.

00:17:57.219 --> 00:17:58.426
- Because a downer can
really bring you down.

00:17:58.426 --> 00:17:59.922
- It just sucks the energy out of it.

00:17:59.922 --> 00:18:01.021
So you go, okay, you know what?

00:18:01.021 --> 00:18:03.140
I can't bring that
downer friend to a party

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.361
or, if I have a party,

00:18:04.361 --> 00:18:06.263
I can only talk to them in limited doses.

00:18:06.263 --> 00:18:07.799
- Right.
- Or they are safe topics.

00:18:07.799 --> 00:18:09.756
So for tanks, you might
have someone who when

00:18:09.756 --> 00:18:11.929
they get around a certain topic

00:18:11.929 --> 00:18:13.121
they get really upset.

00:18:13.121 --> 00:18:15.244
You know that is a no-go topic for them.

00:18:15.244 --> 00:18:17.151
- So don't talk to a tank about politics.

00:18:17.151 --> 00:18:18.275
- Right exactly.

00:18:18.275 --> 00:18:19.689
Or if it's family members.

00:18:19.689 --> 00:18:21.457
So I had people that they're difficult

00:18:21.457 --> 00:18:23.484
but you have to spend time around them

00:18:23.484 --> 00:18:25.718
that you're only spending time
with them on their best days.

00:18:25.718 --> 00:18:27.137
So you know that you know
what they're not good

00:18:27.137 --> 00:18:28.828
in social situations.
- Right.

00:18:28.828 --> 00:18:30.121
- They're much better one-on-one.

00:18:30.121 --> 00:18:30.954
- Right.

00:18:30.954 --> 00:18:33.002
- We're better off going to
a meal or going to coffee.

00:18:33.002 --> 00:18:35.483
So setting up, limits
either on time or topics,

00:18:35.483 --> 00:18:37.088
so they don't become toxic to you

00:18:37.088 --> 00:18:39.387
and that makes it a lot more manageable.

00:18:39.387 --> 00:18:41.788
- Do you also have to watch
not getting caught up in their,

00:18:41.788 --> 00:18:43.255
I mean getting caught up in their drama?

00:18:43.255 --> 00:18:44.581
- Yeah so what's interesting
is there's something

00:18:44.581 --> 00:18:46.536
that called it's called chameleonization.

00:18:46.536 --> 00:18:49.633
Right, so we become like
the person we're with.

00:18:49.633 --> 00:18:50.466
- Right.

00:18:50.466 --> 00:18:51.299
- And so with difficult
people you have to be

00:18:51.299 --> 00:18:53.715
so careful that when you're
with that Debbie downer

00:18:53.715 --> 00:18:56.879
you don't also get into that
critical gossipy complaining.

00:18:56.879 --> 00:18:58.192
- And it's easy to do.

00:18:58.192 --> 00:19:00.836
- Oh it's so because we
want to be congenial.

00:19:00.836 --> 00:19:02.611
- Right.
- And so we're like

00:19:02.611 --> 00:19:05.356
oh if we're angry like them like a tank.

00:19:05.356 --> 00:19:07.212
Or if we're really quiet and a passive.

00:19:07.212 --> 00:19:08.441
But actually that makes
them feel even worse

00:19:08.441 --> 00:19:10.813
because you're both getting
into this really bad area.

00:19:10.813 --> 00:19:13.153
If you can just go into understanding mode

00:19:13.153 --> 00:19:15.102
they actually will come out of their shell

00:19:15.102 --> 00:19:16.902
and they go into their best self.

00:19:16.902 --> 00:19:18.267
- And the passive the same way.

00:19:18.267 --> 00:19:19.100
If you can do that with them?

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.853
- Passive the same way
because most people try to fix

00:19:20.853 --> 00:19:22.576
passes like, one of my good friends,

00:19:22.576 --> 00:19:24.754
she's just very very shy.

00:19:24.754 --> 00:19:26.608
And people always tell her, "Speak up."

00:19:26.608 --> 00:19:28.050
- Oh yeah.
- And that makes

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:28.932
her even more shy.

00:19:28.932 --> 00:19:30.516
So if you ask really specific

00:19:30.516 --> 00:19:32.030
directed questions about what you know

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:34.063
what kind of personal passion
project she's working,

00:19:34.063 --> 00:19:35.840
get her talking about
things she's excited about.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.686
- Yeah.
- Then she's like

00:19:37.686 --> 00:19:41.590
(exhales) and she can relax
and she becomes more active.

